{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-150305-r4518582","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Burgoo","sourcePageId":150305,"sourceRevision":"4518582","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T16:30:50Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Burgoo&oldid=4518582","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:24:46.577Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for stew","Category:Recipes using beef broth and stock","Category:Recipes using carrot","Category:Recipes using celery","Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock","Category:Recipes using corn","Category:Recipes using green bell pepper","Category:Recipes using lima bean","Category:Recipes using meat","Category:Recipes using okra","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Southern U.S. recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"5c719815c050c147f3a7bdeee57fb1f922cf1913dd11528101360f82e4fc7aa7","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Stew recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Burgoo''' is traditional to Western Kentucky and has endless variation. While true tradition burgoo is made from game meats or mutton, modern variation are made from BBQ pork and/or chicken. Recipes range in size from enough to feed a family to a entire community. While cooked meats are used, BBQ meats are preferred for a more authentic taste.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 1 [[Cookbook:pound|pound]] (450 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) mixed cooked [[Cookbook:Meat and poultry|meat]]s ([[Cookbook:beef|beef]], [[Cookbook:lamb|lamb]], [[Cookbook:pork|pork]], [[Cookbook:chicken|chicken]], [[Cookbook:game|game]], etc.)\n* ½ [[Cookbook:gallon|gallon]] (2 [[Cookbook:Liter|liters]]) chicken [[Cookbook:stock|stock]]\n* ½ gallon (2 liters) beef stock\n* 1 [[Cookbook:ounce|ounce]] (30 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:tomato|tomatoes]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n* 1 large [[Cookbook:onion|onion]], diced\n* 1 stalk [[Cookbook:celery|celery]], diced\n* 1 small green [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell pepper]], diced\n* 1 large [[Cookbook:potato|potato]], diced\n* 2 large [[Cookbook:carrot|carrots]], diced\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:pea|peas]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:okra|okra]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Lima Bean|lima beans]]\n* ½ cup yellow [[Cookbook:corn|corn]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoons]] [[Cookbook:garlic|garlic]], [[Cookbook:mincing|minced]]\n* [[Cookbook:salt|Salt]] to taste\n* [[Cookbook:pepper|Pepper]] to taste\n\n==Procedure==\n# Combine all ingredients in a pot, and bring to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]].\n# Reduce heat and [[Cookbook:simmering|simmer]] for 2 hours, skimming the top as needed.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Traditional burgoo was often cooked outdoors in a cast-iron kettle over a wood fire. Purists will insist this greatly improves the flavor.\n\n[[Category:Southern U.S. recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using meat]]\n[[Category:Recipes using okra]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lima bean]]\n[[Category:Recipes using corn]]\n[[Category:Recipes for stew]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef broth and stock]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Burgoo","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 pound (450 g) mixed cooked meats (beef, lamb, pork, chicken, game, etc.)","sourceText":"1 pound (450 g) mixed cooked meats (beef, lamb, pork, chicken, game, etc.)","amountText":"1 pound (450 g) mixed cooked meats (beef, lamb, pork, chicken, game, etc.)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"½ gallon (2 liters) chicken stock","sourceText":"½ gallon (2 liters) chicken stock","amountText":"½ gallon (2 liters) chicken stock","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"½ gallon (2 liters) beef stock","sourceText":"½ gallon (2 liters) beef stock","amountText":"½ gallon (2 liters) beef stock","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 ounce (30 ml) Worcestershire sauce","sourceText":"1 ounce (30 ml) Worcestershire sauce","amountText":"1 ounce (30 ml) Worcestershire sauce","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 cup tomatoes, diced","sourceText":"1 cup tomatoes, diced","amountText":"1 cup tomatoes, diced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 large onion, diced","sourceText":"1 large onion, diced","amountText":"1 large onion, diced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 stalk celery, diced","sourceText":"1 stalk celery, diced","amountText":"1 stalk celery, diced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"1 small green bell pepper, diced","sourceText":"1 small green bell pepper, diced","amountText":"1 small green bell pepper, diced","amount":null,"unit":nu